ENFORCEMENT DECREE OF THE ACT ON PROMOTION OF LINKAGE AND UTILIZATION OF NATIONAL KNOWLEDGE INFORMATION

Article 1 (Purpose)
The purpose of this Decree is to prescribe matters delegated by the Act on Promotion of Linkage and Utilization of National Knowledge Information and matters necessary for its enforcement.

Article 2 (Formulation of Basic Plans, etc.)
(1) Where the Minister of Science and ICT formulates a basic plan for promotion of linkage and utilization of national knowledge information (hereinafter referred to as a "basic plan") under Article 6 (1) of the Act on Promotion of Linkage and Utilization of National Knowledge Information (hereinafter referred to as the "Act"), the Minister shall ensure that the basic plan is linked to the comprehensive plan for an intelligent information society under Article 6 of the Framework Act on Intelligent Informatization. The same shall apply when amending the basic plan.
(2) When the Minister of Science and ICT formulates a basic plan under Article 6 (1) of the Act, the Minister shall publicly announce it in the Official Gazette. The same shall apply when amending the basic plan.

Article 3 (Composition of the National Knowledge Information Committee)
(1) "Vice-ministerial public officials of relevant central administrative agencies prescribed by Presidential Decree, including the Vice Minister of Finance and Economy, Vice Minister of Education, Vice Minister of the Interior and Safety, Vice Minister of Culture, Sports and Tourism, and Vice Minister of Planning and Budget" in Article 8 (3) 1 of the Act means the following persons: <Amended on October 1, 2025; December 30, 2025>
1. The Vice Minister of Finance and Economy;
2. The Vice Minister of Education;
3. The Vice Minister of the Interior and Safety;
4. The Vice Minister of Culture, Sports and Tourism;
5. The Vice Minister of Agriculture, Food and Rural Affairs;
6. The Vice Minister of Trade and Industry;
7. The Vice Minister of Health and Welfare;
8. The Vice Minister of Climate, Energy and Environment;
9. The Vice Minister of Employment and Labor;
10. The Vice Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport;
11. The Vice Minister of Oceans and Fisheries;
11-2. The Vice Minister of Planning and Budget;
12. Other vice-ministerial public officials of relevant central administrative agencies commissioned by the Minister of Science and ICT upon determining that their participation as members of the National Knowledge Information Committee under Article 8 (1) of the Act (hereinafter referred to as the "Committee") is necessary.
(2) The Minister of Science and ICT may dismiss a Committee member under Article 8 (3) 2 of the Act where the member falls under any of the following subparagraphs:
1. Where the member becomes unable to perform duties due to a physical or mental disability;
2. Where the member has committed misconduct related to duties;
3. Where the member is deemed unsuitable as a member due to neglect of duties, damage to dignity, or other reasons;
4. Where the member fails to recuse himself or herself despite falling under any subparagraph of Article 4 (1);
5. Where the member expresses that it is difficult to perform duties.

Article 4 (Exclusion, Challenge, and Recusal of Committee Members)
(1) A Committee member falling under any of the following subparagraphs shall be excluded from deliberation and resolution on a dispute mediation case referred to the Committee pursuant to the main clause of Article 21 (1) of the Act (hereinafter referred to as a "dispute mediation case" in this Article):
1. Where the Committee member, the member's spouse, or a person who was the member's spouse is a party to the dispute mediation case or is a joint holder of rights or joint obligor in relation to that case;
2. Where the Committee member is or was a relative of a party to the dispute mediation case;
3. Where the Committee member has provided testimony, an appraisal, or legal advice concerning the dispute mediation case;
4. Where the Committee member is or was involved in the dispute mediation case as an agent of a party.
(2) A party to a dispute mediation case may challenge a Committee member before the Committee where a ground for exclusion specified in any subparagraph of paragraph (1) exists or there are circumstances that make it difficult to expect fair deliberation and resolution from the member; the Committee shall decide by resolution whether to accept the challenge. In such cases, the member subject to the challenge shall not participate in that resolution.
(3) Where a Committee member falls under a ground for exclusion specified in any subparagraph of paragraph (1), the member shall voluntarily recuse himself or herself from deliberation and resolution on that dispute mediation case.

Article 5 (Operation of the Committee)
(1) The chairperson of the Committee shall convene and preside over its meetings.
(2) Where the chairperson of the Committee is unable to perform duties for an unavoidable reason, members under Article 8 (3) 2 of the Act designated in advance by the chairperson shall act on the chairperson's behalf in the order of such designation.
(3) The Committee shall have one executive secretary to handle its affairs, who shall be designated by the chairperson of the Committee from among public officials belonging to the Senior Civil Service responsible for promoting linkage and utilization of national knowledge information in the Ministry of Science and ICT.
(4) Where the chairperson of the Committee intends to convene a meeting, the chairperson shall notify each member in writing (including electronic documents) of the date, time, place, and agenda of the meeting no later than seven days before the meeting date: Provided, That in urgent circumstances or for an unavoidable reason, notification may be given no later than the day before the meeting date.
(5) Where the chairperson of the Committee deems it necessary for deliberation and resolution on matters specified in the subparagraphs of Article 9 (1) of the Act, the chairperson may have relevant experts or persons responsible for affairs concerning national knowledge information at State agencies, etc. under subparagraph 1 of Article 2 of the Act (hereinafter referred to as "State agencies, etc.") attend a meeting and hear their opinions.
(6) Meetings of the Committee shall be convened with a majority of its incumbent members present, and resolutions shall be adopted with the affirmative votes of a majority of the members present.

Article 6 (Composition and Operation of Expert Committees)
(1) The Committee may establish the following expert committees under Article 8 (5) of the Act, following a resolution of the Committee:
1. An expert committee for preliminary investigation, review, etc. of the Committee's dispute mediation duties under Article 21 of the Act (hereinafter referred to as the "Expert Committee on Dispute Mediation");
2. Other expert committees for preliminary investigation, review, etc. of agenda items in specialized fields, including improvement of systems related to national knowledge information and standardization of national knowledge information.
(2) The Expert Committee on Dispute Mediation shall consist of not more than 10 members commissioned by the chairperson of the Committee from among the following persons, with consideration given to gender, and the chairperson of the Committee shall designate the chairperson of the Expert Committee on Dispute Mediation from among its members:
1. Persons falling under either of the following items:
(a) Public officials in the Senior Civil Service of the Ministry of Science and ICT who are or have been responsible for duties related to national knowledge information;
(b) Persons who are or have been employed by a dedicated agency under Article 11 (1) of the Act, State agencies, etc., or a business operators' association, and have experience in duties concerning the linkage and utilization of national knowledge information;
2. Persons who have served as judges, prosecutors, attorneys-at-law, or patent attorneys for at least five years;
3. Persons who hold or have held a position of associate professor or higher, or an equivalent position, at a university or an accredited research institution;
4. Other persons recognized by the Minister of Science and ICT as having extensive knowledge and experience concerning the linkage and utilization of national knowledge information.
(3) An expert committee under paragraph (1) 2 shall consist of not more than 10 members commissioned by the chairperson of the Committee from among technical, legal, or other experts in the relevant specialized field, with consideration given to gender, and the chairperson of the Committee shall designate the chairperson of the expert committee from among its members.
(4) The term of office of expert committee members shall be two years, and they may be reappointed for only one consecutive term: Provided, That the term of office of a member newly commissioned due to the resignation of another member or other such reason shall be the remainder of the predecessor's term.
(5) The chairperson of an expert committee shall convene and preside over meetings: Provided, That where the chairperson is unable to perform duties for an unavoidable reason, members shall act on the chairperson's behalf in the order designated in advance by the chairperson.
(6) Where the chairperson of an expert committee intends to convene a meeting of the expert committee, the chairperson shall notify each member in writing (including electronic documents) of the date, time, place, and agenda no later than seven days before the meeting: Provided, That in urgent circumstances or for an unavoidable reason, such notification may be given no later than the day preceding the meeting.
(7) The chairperson of an expert committee shall report the results to the Committee after holding a meeting of the expert committee.

Article 7 (Allowances and Travel Expenses for the Committee, etc.)
Allowances and travel expenses may be paid, within budgetary limits, to members, relevant experts, or other relevant persons attending meetings of the Committee or an expert committee: Provided, That this shall not apply to public officials attending in direct connection with duties under their jurisdiction.

Article 8 (Detailed Operating Rules)
Matters necessary for the operation of the Committee, etc., other than those provided for in this Decree, shall be prescribed by the chairperson of the Committee following a resolution of the Committee, and matters necessary for the composition and operation of an expert committee, etc. shall be prescribed by the chairperson of the expert committee following a resolution of that expert committee.

Article 9 (Duties of Dedicated Agencies)
"Duties prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 11 (1) 4 of the Act means the following duties:
1. Duties supporting the formulation and implementation of policies related to national knowledge information;
2. Duties supporting the operation of the consultative body under Article 12 (4) of the Act;
3. Duties supporting dispute mediation under Article 21 of the Act;
4. Other duties deemed necessary by the Minister of Science and ICT to promote the linkage and utilization of national knowledge information.

Article 10 (Operation of Dedicated Agencies)
(1) A dedicated agency under Article 11 (1) of the Act (hereinafter referred to as a "dedicated agency") shall establish a separate account to manage funds received as contributions under paragraph (2) of the same Article.
(2) Matters necessary for the operation of dedicated agencies, etc., other than those provided for in paragraph (1), shall be prescribed by the Minister of Science and ICT.

Article 11 (Designation and Operation of Knowledge Information Centers, etc.)
(1) An institution seeking designation as a knowledge information center under Article 12 (1) of the Act shall meet all of the following requirements and apply to the Minister of Science and ICT for designation:
1. It shall be a State agency, etc.;
2. Expertise in the production, holding, management, etc. of national knowledge information in the relevant field;
3. Capacity to provide services to the public using national knowledge information in the relevant field;
4. Other requirements deemed necessary by the Minister of Science and ICT for the efficient linkage and utilization of national knowledge information.
(2) To promote the operation of a knowledge information center designated under Article 12 (1) of the Act (hereinafter referred to as a "knowledge information center"), the head of the center shall formulate operating guidelines taking the following matters into consideration and notify the Minister of Science and ICT thereof:
1. Matters concerning technical and managerial measures for linking national knowledge information to the integrated platform;
2. Matters concerning ensuring the currency, accuracy, and reliability of national knowledge information;
3. Matters concerning standardization for the production, linkage, and efficient utilization of national knowledge information;
4. Matters concerning personnel management at the knowledge information center;
5. Other matters deemed necessary for the efficient linkage and utilization of national knowledge information.

Article 12 (Composition and Operation of the Consultative Body)
(1) The consultative body under Article 12 (4) of the Act (hereinafter referred to as the "consultative body") shall be composed of the following institutions or organizations:
1. The dedicated agency;
2. Knowledge information centers;
3. Other institutions or organizations whose participation in the consultative body is deemed necessary by the Minister of Science and ICT to promote the provision and use of national knowledge information.
(2) The consultative body shall consult on the following matters:
1. Matters concerning policies and projects related to national knowledge information;
2. Matters concerning policies for linkage with the integrated platform;
3. Matters concerning cooperation between the private and public sectors;
4. Other matters deemed necessary to promote the linkage and utilization of national knowledge information.
(3) The Minister of Science and ICT and the heads of State agencies, etc. shall endeavor to ensure that opinions presented by the consultative body are reflected in policies related to national knowledge information.
(4) Matters necessary for the operation of the consultative body, other than those prescribed in paragraphs (1) through (3), shall be determined by the Minister of Science and ICT.

Article 13 (Criteria and Procedures for Designation of National Knowledge Information for Linkage with the Integrated Platform)
(1) Where the Minister of Science and ICT intends to designate national knowledge information for linkage with the integrated platform pursuant to Article 13 (1) of the Act, the Minister shall take the following matters into account:
1. The purposes of and grounds for linkage of national knowledge information;
2. The types and content of national knowledge information to be linked;
3. The current status of national knowledge information holdings and linkage plans;
4. The expected effects of linkage of national knowledge information;
5. Other matters necessary to promote the linkage and utilization of national knowledge information.
(2) Where the head of a State agency, etc. seeks designation of national knowledge information held by the agency, etc. for linkage with the integrated platform pursuant to Article 13 (1) of the Act, the head shall prepare documents stating the matters specified in the subparagraphs of paragraph (1) and request consultation with the Minister of Science and ICT on the designation.

Article 14 (Formulation of Plans for Linkage with and Utilization of the Integrated Platform) Plans concerning the digitization of national knowledge information and linkage with and utilization of the integrated platform, etc. under Article 13 (2) of the Act shall include the following matters:
1. Matters concerning the management and digitization of national knowledge information to be linked;
2. Matters concerning technical measures for linkage with and utilization of the integrated platform;
3. Matters concerning standardization for the linkage and utilization of national knowledge information;
4. Other matters necessary for the digitization of national knowledge information and linkage with and utilization of the integrated platform, etc.

Article 15 (Establishment and Operation of the Integrated Platform, etc.)
(1) Where the Minister of Science and ICT establishes and operates the integrated platform pursuant to Article 14 (1) of the Act, the Minister shall take the following matters into account:
1. Integrated search functions for national knowledge information;
2. Functions for the systematic collection and management of classification systems (referring to the systematic classification or organization of national knowledge information according to structured criteria for the systematic management and utilization of national knowledge information; hereinafter the same shall apply) and metadata (referring to data representing the structure, attributes, etc. of national knowledge information for its systematic management and convenient retrieval and utilization; hereinafter the same shall apply) for the linkage of national knowledge information;
3. The usefulness, accessibility, and ease of use of national knowledge information;
4. Other matters necessary for the provision, linkage, and utilization of national knowledge information.
(2) The Minister of Science and ICT shall ensure that national knowledge information linked to the integrated platform is kept current and accurate and that its interconnectivity is maintained.
(3) The Minister of Science and ICT shall enable users of the integrated platform to report difficulties, etc. and may, where necessary to resolve such difficulties, etc., request corrective action, etc. from the head of the relevant State agency, etc.

Article 16 (Status Surveys)
(1) The Minister of Science and ICT shall conduct the status survey under Article 15 (1) of the Act (hereinafter referred to as a "status survey") regularly every year and may conduct additional status surveys as necessary.
(2) A status survey shall include the following matters:
1. Matters concerning the current status of national knowledge information holdings;
2. Matters concerning the current status of systems providing national knowledge information;
3. Matters concerning the current status of linkage with the integrated platform;
4. Matters concerning the current status of standardization of classification systems and metadata for national knowledge information;
5. Matters concerning the current status of the use of national knowledge information through the integrated platform;
6. Matters concerning the utilization of national knowledge information, including statistics on its use and user satisfaction surveys;
7. Other matters deemed to require a survey concerning the current status of national knowledge information holdings and linkage with the integrated platform.
(3) Where the Minister of Science and ICT conducts a status survey under paragraph (1), the Minister shall report the results to the Committee.

Article 17 (Establishment and Implementation of Standards, etc.)
(1) To promote the standardization of national knowledge information pursuant to Article 17 (1) of the Act, the Minister of Science and ICT shall establish and implement standards for the following matters:
1. Methods for creating and managing metadata for national knowledge information;
2. Methods of linkage of national knowledge information;
3. Other matters necessary for the production, linkage, and efficient utilization of national knowledge information.
(2) When establishing standards under paragraph (1), the Minister of Science and ICT shall undergo deliberation and resolution by the Committee.
(3) The Minister of Science and ICT shall announce in the Official Gazette the national knowledge information standards that have undergone deliberation and resolution by the Committee under paragraph (2) and make them public on the website of the Ministry of Science and ICT.
(4) To standardize national knowledge information pursuant to Article 17 (2) of the Act, the Minister of Science and ICT may undertake the following duties:
1. Surveys, research, and development related to domestic and foreign standards for national knowledge information;
2. Cooperation with international standards organizations and international standards institutions related to standards for national knowledge information;
3. Other matters necessary for the standardization of national knowledge information.
(5) The heads of State agencies, etc. shall endeavor to comply with the standards under paragraph (1).

Article 18 (Cooperation with Private Sector)
(1) Where the Minister of Science and ICT provides national knowledge information through private business operators and associations of private business operators (hereinafter referred to as "private business operators, etc.") under Article 18 (1) of the Act, the Minister shall ensure that users of national knowledge information can ascertain the following matters:
1. Matters concerning the sources of national knowledge information;
2. Matters concerning the titles, authors, publishing institutions, publication dates, etc. of national knowledge information;
3. Other matters necessary to promote the use of national knowledge information.
(2) Where the Minister of Science and ICT intends to link knowledge information held by the private sector that is worth preserving and using (hereinafter referred to as "private knowledge information" in this Article) with the integrated platform under Article 18 (2) of the Act, the Minister shall consult in advance with the private business operators, etc. holding that private knowledge information concerning the following matters:
1. Matters concerning the private knowledge information to be linked;
2. Matters concerning the methods, etc. of linking private knowledge information with the integrated platform;
3. Matters concerning rights in private knowledge information, such as copyright, or the processing of personal information, etc.;
4. Matters concerning the bearing of expenses arising from the linkage and use, etc. of private knowledge information;
5. Other matters necessary to link private knowledge information with the integrated platform and promote the use of private knowledge information.
(3) The Minister of Science and ICT may establish and operate a system of cooperation with private business operators, etc. concerning publicity and related activities to identify national knowledge information and private knowledge information and promote their use.

Article 19 (Requests for Dispute Mediation and Processing Period)
(1) Upon receiving a request for dispute mediation from a party to a dispute over the linkage and utilization of national knowledge information under Article 21 (1) of the Act, the Committee shall inform the other party of the contents of the request.
(2) The Committee shall examine the contents of the request and prepare a mediation proposal within 30 days from the date it receives a request for dispute mediation under paragraph (1): Provided, That, where unavoidable circumstances exist, the processing period may be extended by resolution of the Committee.
(3) Where the Committee extends the processing period under the proviso to paragraph (2), it shall notify the requester without delay of the reasons and the expected processing period.

Article 20 (Mediation of Disputes)
(1) The Minister of Science and ICT may have public officials under his or her jurisdiction conduct fact-finding investigations concerning dispute mediation cases.
(2) A public official conducting a fact-finding investigation under paragraph (1) may request State agencies, etc. to submit materials for the investigation and may, where necessary, request their cooperation for an on-site investigation.
(3) Requests for submission of materials or for cooperation under paragraph (2) shall be made within the scope necessary for dispute mediation.
(4) Where necessary, the Committee may have the person requesting dispute mediation and the officers in charge of the relevant affairs at State agencies, etc. attend to hear their opinions.
(5) Where necessary, the Committee may, in consultation with the person requesting dispute mediation and State agencies, etc., recommend an agreement concerning the provision or use of national knowledge information.
(6) The Committee shall prepare a mediation proposal in consideration of the findings of the fact-finding investigations and the opinions under paragraphs (1) through (4), and shall provide the mediation proposal to each party without delay.
(7) Where a party who has received a mediation proposal under paragraph (6) does not indicate whether to accept it within 15 days from the date of receipt, the party shall be deemed to have rejected mediation.
(8) Where the parties accept the mediation proposal, the Committee shall prepare a written mediation agreement, which shall be signed by the chairperson of the Committee and each party.

Article 21 (Inspections of Linkage and Utilization of National Knowledge Information, etc.)
(1) The Minister of Science and ICT shall inspect the actual state of linkage and utilization of national knowledge information annually under Article 22 (1) of the Act and may conduct additional inspections whenever necessary.
(2) Where the Minister of Science and ICT intends to conduct an inspection of actual conditions under paragraph (1) (hereinafter referred to as a "status inspection"), the Minister shall establish a status inspection plan that includes the following matters:
1. The purpose of the status inspection;
2. The subjects and content of the status inspection;
3. The date and methods of the status inspection;
4. Other matters necessary for the status inspection.
(3) Where necessary for a status inspection of national knowledge information, the Minister of Science and ICT may request State agencies, etc. (excluding the National Assembly, courts, the Constitutional Court, and the National Election Commission; hereinafter the same shall apply in this Article) to submit relevant materials.
(4) When notifying the results of a status inspection under Article 22 (2) of the Act, the Minister of Science and ICT may request the head of the relevant State agency, etc. to take necessary measures within 30 days from the date of receipt of the notification and to notify the Minister of Science and ICT of the results of those measures.
(5) The Minister of Science and ICT may request the head of a State agency, etc. that has not completed the corrective measures under paragraph (4) to submit the reasons and a plan for future measures.

